--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Served the repository root with python3 -m http.server and drove the page in headless
Chromium (chrome-headless-shell over the DevTools protocol), at 1280px and 390px:

  - every section exercised: board operations, makeActive tabs, drawer, reveal,
    accordion, easing lab, filter sliders and pulse, centring, overlay, scroll lock,
    tag removal / exclusion / array form / Enter constraint / detach, countdown,
    breakpoints, random, IO.get (3 files, progress 100%, status true), all 12 bad-input
    buttons and all 9 defect buttons
  - no console errors on load; the only console output during the run is the expected
    console.error from the slide.toRight({ colour }) defect button
  - no horizontal overflow at 390px (scrollWidth == innerWidth)
  - screenshots checked for the hero, motion, layout, events and data sections

Not checked: a real (non-headless) browser, clipboard.copy (needs a real user gesture),
and browserType() in Chrome proper. Headless Chrome's user agent is not recognised and
throws, which the page catches and shows.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFECTS FOUND, RECORDED NOT FIXED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

See doc/core.md "Known defects". Main ones: scroll.x()/y() without true throws;
makeActive without a parent never clears the previous element; $$.scroll.direction(),
$$.IO.save(), browserResizeProperty getters and validatePhoneNumber throw;
camelToCSSstandard returns "undefined" in place of capitals; randomString can drop
characters; ScreenBreakPoint requires both keys despite having defaults; core.css overlay
rule lacks left:0 and matches every child div; $$.delay is a busy-wait; filter() with
options leaves its transition and listener behind; toRight/toTop/toBottom log invalid
options instead of throwing.
